{"The URL is interpolated directly into an HTML attribute and link text without escaping, so a crafted URL containing quotes or HTML can inject arbitrary HTML/JavaScript into the page": 0.9339991807937622, "The code assumes every RSS item has a `content` field and calls `scrub` on it directly; if `i.content` is nil, this will raise a NoMethodError and abort the whole polling job": 0.970425009727478, "If the container element is missing from the page, `comments` will be `null` and calling `appendChild` on it will throw a runtime error": 0.9542751312255859, "Using JavaScript-style Sprockets directives (`//= require`) in an `.scss` stylesheet means these lines are treated as comments by Sass and are not executed as dependency imports, so `normalize` and `base` will not actually be included": 0.3155903220176697, "The referer host comparison is case-sensitive, so a valid embeddable host differing only by letter case will be rejected, incorrectly blocking legitimate embeds": 0.3213437497615814, "The `cook` method calls `cook_method` but there is no attribute or method named `cook_method` defined in this model, so this will raise a NoMethodError at runtime when saving posts": 0.03053412027657032, "The post revision call passes a raw string where the reviser API typically expects a hash of fields, which will cause runtime errors or silently fail to update the post": 0.22195854783058167, "The remote import path fetches content from whatever URL is provided without even a basic scheme check, so a crafted `url` using non-HTTP schemes could be used to read local resources or trigger SSRF-style access to internal services": 0.860164999961853, "The inline script lacks a CSP nonce, so on instances with a strict Content-Security-Policy that only allows scripts with a valid nonce, this reload logic will be blocked by the browser": 0.11794744431972504, "The `embed_url` column is declared as a plain string, which defaults to a 255-character limit; longer embed URLs will be silently truncated, potentially causing incorrect uniqueness collisions": 0.9087110757827759, "Using `force: true` on the table creation will drop the `top_topics` table if it already exists, causing unintended data loss if this migration is ever rerun": 0.7304389476776123, "Using the non-bang save without checking its return value means validation failures will be silently ignored while later logic still runs as if the record was persisted": 0.6685580611228943, "The host comparison in TopicRetriever is case-sensitive because `SiteSetting.embeddable_host` is compared directly to `URI(@embed_url).host`, which is typically lowercase": 0.76662278175354, "The test example that asserts no retrieval when the embed URL is invalid does not stub the embeddable host, making the test non-isolated and potentially flaky": 0.5375620126724243, "The 'requires feed_polling_enabled?' example does not stub the URL and username settings to valid values, so the job might early-return for other reasons": 0.5170936584472656, "The 'requires feed_polling_url' example does not ensure the enabled flag and username are valid, so the job may skip polling due to those settings instead of the missing URL": 0.5430474281311035, "The 'requires embed_by_username' example omits stubbing the enabled flag and URL to valid values, so polling might be skipped for those reasons": 0.5692826509475708, "The test for malformed URLs asserts that the total record count is exactly zero, which makes the example depend on global database state instead of only verifying that the import did not create a new record": 0.7830809950828552}